msgid "about.controls"
msgstr "Controls"

msgid "about.controls_detail"
msgstr "Xbox: A selects and B goes back. PlayStation: Cross selects and Circle goes back. Switch: B selects and A goes back, as in the game's own menus. A controller set up in Ember: the button you chose for Light kick selects and the one you chose for Medium kick goes back, whatever its button layout. Keyboard: arrows, Enter and Escape. The D-pad moves; Left and Right change a value. Going back at Home hides Ember. F10, or Start on a controller, opens it again at the game's main menu.\n\nIn a room, A on a table lets you pick a seat, A on your own seat readies up, and B leaves your seat or queue place (on other controllers, the buttons in the same places). On Xbox, X opens Fighter, Y opens Options and View opens Chat; press it again to return to the room. PlayStation uses Square, Triangle and Share or Create; Switch uses Y, X and Minus.\n\nIn training, F6 opens the controls, F5 hides the HUD, F7 records and F8 plays. On a controller, hold View (Share, Create or Minus) and press Start."

msgid "about.controls_keyboard"
msgstr "On the keyboard, Space also selects and Backspace also goes back. In a room, F opens Fighter, T opens Options and C opens Chat. Escape always goes back, even on your own seat; Delete leaves your seat or queue place."

